# One IPv4 CIDR per line. Requests from an IP inside one of these ranges are
# counted, for connection-limit purposes, as coming from the whole CIDR
# instead of the individual IP. Use this for ISPs that NAT many real users
# through a fast-rotating shared IP pool, which otherwise makes a single
# legit user look like many devices.
# Lines starting with # are ignored. Reloaded automatically every 5 minutes.
# This file is shipped and updated with Libertea itself (via git), since
# it lives outside the gitignored data/ folder.
#
# Delta Telecom Ltd (AS29049, Azerbaijan) - some Iranian ISPs NAT users
# through this network, rotating their public IP on every request.
# Source: RIPEstat announced-prefixes for AS29049, collapsed to minimal
# supernets, fetched 2026-09-11. Re-check periodically, ranges can change:
# https://stat.ripe.net/data/announced-prefixes/data.json?resource=AS29049
